From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:14:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] Android: move the cursor on presses that arrive without
 a motion event

Touch and stylus presses have no preceding motion, so tools acted at the
previous press position.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PMkXiZQmqtvCJRtsVHJjyT
---
 common/view/wx_view_controls.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common/view/wx_view_controls.cpp b/common/view/wx_view_controls.cpp
index f66d3ae8..d765c8a2 100644
--- a/common/view/wx_view_controls.cpp
+++ b/common/view/wx_view_controls.cpp
@@ -584,6 +584,13 @@ void WX_VIEW_CONTROLS::setState( STATE aNewState )
 
 void WX_VIEW_CONTROLS::onButton( wxMouseEvent& aEvent )
 {
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+    // Touch and stylus presses arrive without a preceding motion event, so the press itself
+    // has to move the cursor or tools act at wherever the previous press left it
+    if( aEvent.ButtonDown() && m_state == IDLE )
+        m_cursorPos = GetClampedCoords( m_view->ToWorld( VECTOR2D( aEvent.GetX(), aEvent.GetY() ) ) );
+#endif
+
     switch( m_state )
     {
     case IDLE:
